WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.976
A metal spoon, a glass
window, a bottle of petrol.

2
00:00:08.196 --> 00:00:11.493
All three came out of
rocks, deep in planet Earth.

3
00:00:11.993 --> 00:00:15.197
Every material we use
comes from planet Earth.

4
00:00:15.417 --> 00:00:19.458
There is nowhere else.
Not the Moon, not the Sun.

5
00:00:19.678 --> 00:00:22.000
Wood and wool come from living things.

6
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.099
Metal, glass, oil and gas come from rocks.

7
00:00:25.319 --> 00:00:30.056
So there are two sources: the
rocks, and the living things on top.

8
00:00:30.556 --> 00:00:33.435
Metal is found inside rocks called ores.

9
00:00:33.655 --> 00:00:37.417
The rock is dug up and heated,
and the metal is separated out.

10
00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.237
That is where the metal
in your spoon began.

11
00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:44.498
Glass is melted sand, and
sand is tiny bits of rock.

12
00:00:44.718 --> 00:00:47.783
Bricks are baked clay.
Clay is a soft rock.

13
00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:52.230
Oil and natural gas are trapped
deep in rocks underground.

14
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:55.004
The oil is pumped up to the surface.

15
00:00:55.224 --> 00:00:58.614
Some of it is made into
petrol, and cars burn it.

16
00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:03.757
Some becomes plastic. So even a
plastic bottle began in the Earth.

17
00:01:04.257 --> 00:01:07.369
Millions of years ago,
a fish swims in the sea.

18
00:01:07.589 --> 00:01:11.211
It dies, and sinks into
the soft mud at the bottom.

19
00:01:11.431 --> 00:01:14.542
More mud settles on
top, layer after layer.

20
00:01:14.762 --> 00:01:20.056
The weight squashes the mud into rock,
with the fish's shape pressed inside.

21
00:01:20.276 --> 00:01:23.667
One day the rock splits
open, and there is the fish.

22
00:01:23.887 --> 00:01:30.481
Not the fish itself. Its shape, pressed
in like a footprint. That is a fossil.

23
00:01:30.981 --> 00:01:34.371
Where would you look for a
fossil? You can look it up.

24
00:01:34.591 --> 00:01:39.932
A fact card is a secondary source. Somebody
found it out and wrote it down for you.

25
00:01:40.152 --> 00:01:45.074
Fossils are found in rock made of
layers of mud or sand, like sandstone.

26
00:01:45.294 --> 00:01:51.285
Most are hard parts: shells, bones and
teeth. A jellyfish rarely leaves one.

27
00:01:51.505 --> 00:01:56.335
Look at cliffs and beaches. Go with a
grown-up, and never stand under a cliff.

28
00:01:56.835 --> 00:02:00.736
A quarry cuts rock out of a
hillside, and leaves a huge hole.

29
00:02:00.956 --> 00:02:05.693
A spill can cover beaches and birds
in oil, so it is done very carefully.

30
00:02:05.913 --> 00:02:09.210
Recycle a can, and less
rock has to be dug up.

31
00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:14.074
A geologist studies rocks. A
palaeontologist studies fossils.

32
00:02:14.294 --> 00:02:17.313
Science helps us see the
harm, and do less of it.

33
00:02:17.813 --> 00:02:20.552
Everything you use
comes from planet Earth.

34
00:02:20.772 --> 00:02:25.231
Metal from ore, glass from
sand, oil from deep in the rock.

35
00:02:25.451 --> 00:02:29.491
A fossil is the shape of something
once alive, kept in rock.

36
00:02:29.711 --> 00:02:33.426
Look it up, and recycle.
Then less has to be dug up.
